			<li>Accommodation arrangements</li>
			<li>Airport pickup and drop-off coordination</li>
			<li>Language translation services</li>
			<li>Post-treatment follow-up assistance</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>What Is the Difference Between a Hospital and a Medical Tourism Facilitator?</h2>
		<p>
			A hospital provides medical diagnosis, treatment, surgical procedures, and patient care, whereas a medical
			tourism facilitator helps international patients coordinate their medical travel and hospital-related
			arrangements. Both have different roles in supporting a patient's medical journey.
		</p>

